# Liara deploy (explicit ask only)

**Never** deploy unless the user clearly asks (e.g. “deploy”, “ship to Liara”). Agent mode / commit / push do **not** imply deploy.

Production: Liara app **`inbox`**, domain **`inboxs.ir`**. Never Railway. Prefer GitHub Actions; local `liara deploy` only if Actions is unavailable (say so first).

## Build location order (locked)

Liara CLI `--build-location` only accepts **`iran`** | **`germany`** (no France option today).

1. **Iran first** — primary path in `deploy.yml` (full-source `Dockerfile` on Iran).
2. **Germany second** — only if Iran did not succeed (prebuilt `Dockerfile.runtime` on Germany).
3. Do **not** invent a France build path until Liara documents it.

## Hard lesson (Sep 2026)

Liara’s “Release created” / container health and a green Actions job can still leave **public 502**. Actions green ≠ site up. **Never tell the user deploy succeeded until a live probe passes.** If the app is dead after deploy, say clearly: **“Production is DOWN (502 / health failed).”** Do not soft-pedal.

Germany releases have been healthy-but-502 while Iran full-source restored public traffic — that is why Iran is primary.

## When the user asks to deploy

1. Push deployable commits to GitHub `main` if ahead.
2. Prefer green CI for that SHA if still running; otherwise `deploy.yml` smoke gate covers it.
3. Trigger and watch:

```bash
gh workflow run deploy.yml --ref main
gh run watch "$(gh run list --workflow=deploy.yml --limit 1 --json databaseId -q '.[0].databaseId')"
```

4. Confirm workflow success (**Deploy succeeded** + **Verify live inboxs.ir** must both be **green**, not skipped). Report Actions URL / SHA / path (Iran primary vs Germany fallback).
5. **Mandatory live probe** (even if the workflow already probed — agent double-check):

```bash
# Expect HTTP 200 and JSON ok:true / db:up. Retry ~2 min (15s interval) after release.
curl -sS -o /tmp/inbox-health -w '%{http_code}' --max-time 20 https://inboxs.ir/api/health
curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' --max-time 20 https://inboxs.ir
curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' --max-time 20 https://inbox.liara.run
```

   - **Pass:** health body has `"ok":true` (and preferably `"db":"up"`) and homepage is not 502.
   - **Fail (502 / 000 / non-ok):** tell the user **Production is DOWN**. Retry Iran (do not stop after one green Germany release):

```bash
gh workflow run liara-iran-deploy.yml --ref main
gh run watch "$(gh run list --workflow=liara-iran-deploy.yml --limit 1 --json databaseId -q '.[0].databaseId')"
# Re-run the live probe. Only then call the site up.
```

6. **Mandatory local DB dump** (Actions backup → download; local Liara CLI auth often broken):

```bash
gh workflow run backup-db.yml --ref main
# wait, then:
gh run download <BACKUP_RUN_ID> -n inbox-db-local-backup -D backups/tmp-dl
mv backups/tmp-dl/*.dump "backups/inbox-db-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S).dump"
rm -rf backups/tmp-dl
```

Report absolute dump path. Deploy is not done until dump exists **and** live probe passed.
7. If workflow, Iran retry, live probe, or backup fails after recovery attempts — **stop and tell the user**. Do not claim success.

Requires repo secret `LIARA_API_TOKEN`.

## Runtime image (Germany fallback path)

`Dockerfile.runtime` (Debian slim) **must** `apt-get install openssl ca-certificates` before Prisma. Missing OpenSSL matched Liara Prisma warnings and dead containers. Do not remove that layer. Full-source `Dockerfile` already installs openssl on Alpine.

## What `deploy.yml` does

- Manual `workflow_dispatch` only; one deploy at a time (`cancel-in-progress: false`).
- CI green → skip smoke; else smoke gate.
- **Primary:** full-source `Dockerfile` → Liara **Iran**.
- **Fallback:** if Iran job fails → Actions-built Nitro → `Dockerfile.runtime` → Liara **Germany**.
- **Verify live:** after a successful path, curl `https://inboxs.ir/api/health` until 200/`ok` or fail the workflow. Must not be skipped when a deploy path succeeded.
- If verify fails: agent runs `liara-iran-deploy.yml` and re-probes.
- No GHCR/`--image`. No BuildKit `--mount` on Liara-built Dockerfiles.

Do not invent a path that skips Actions, smoke/CI, live probe, or the local dump.
